<title>FINLAND: Finland says has first euro-denominated EIB loan.</title>
<headline>Finland says has first euro-denominated EIB loan.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Finland and the European Investment Bank (EIB) on Friday signed the first loan agreement ever for both parties to be nominated in euros, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>The 20-year loan to buy ice-breakers was worth the equivalent of 155 million markka ($30 million).</p>
<p>&quot;The ice-breaker loan is historic. It is the first granted by the EIB in euros and at the same time it is the first taken by Finland in euros,&quot; the ministry said.</p>
<p>Finland and the EIB also signed a new 230 million markka 20-year loan agreement for road construction, and a deal on the final 400 million markka portion of an earlier granted 1.15 billion markka 20-year road loan, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi ($ = 5.178 Finnish Markka)</p>
